2.3. Functional Requirements
The following table lists the Functional Requirements (FRs) of the AR-IMMS system, grouped by module. Each item should be assigned a code (FR01, FR02, …) to support the Requirement Traceability Matrix in Section 2.9:
FR01–FR03 — Authentication
Login/logout, JWT-based authentication, password change.
FR04–FR05 — User Management
Create/edit/delete user accounts, assign roles (Admin/Operator/Technician).
FR06–FR07 — Infrastructure Management
Manage the Site → Room → Rack → Server → Container hierarchy.
FR08 — Telemetry
Collect and store real-time CPU/RAM/Disk/Network data.
FR09–FR10 — Alert
Automatically detect anomalies based on thresholds; manage the alert lifecycle (OPEN → ACKNOWLEDGED → RESOLVED → CLOSED).
FR11 — Incident
Create an incident from an alert when formal handling is required.
FR12–FR13 — Ticket
Create, assign to a technician, and update ticket status (OPEN → IN_PROGRESS → RESOLVED → CLOSED).
FR14 — Maintenance
Record maintenance results (description, time, technician involved).
FR15 — Digital Twin
Synchronize the physical device's status with its digital representation in real time.
FR16–FR17 — AR
Scan QR/ArUco markers to identify devices; display an overlay of information (telemetry, alerts, tickets) on the mobile device.
